# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — agent operating manual

{{PROJECT_DESCRIPTION}}

This file is loaded into **every** agent session in this repo, so it is
deliberately short. Elaboration lives in the articles below, which an agent
loads on demand.

## The article layer

- `constitution/shared-invariants.md` — the portable framework rules: specs
  before code, vertical slices, tests as the target function, fresh context per
  phase, standards findings separated from behavior findings, human-in-the-loop
  by label, no autonomous merge, executable process docs, measured ceilings,
  refactor/behavior separation, context budget. Read it once per project, not
  once per task. **This file is shared-layer** (see `VERSION`): it is copied
  verbatim from the kit and is not edited here — a local exception belongs in a
  local article instead.

## Local rules

Your stack-specific and process-specific rules go here — the concrete mechanism
for each shared invariant that needs one. K1 (#3) ships `local-engineering` and
`local-workflow` article templates for this section; until then, write them
inline or leave this section empty rather than letting the shared article carry
local vocabulary.

## The gate

Every rule in this manual must be executable or CI-verified — a rule nothing
checks decays into a lie (shared invariant §8).

- `scripts/check.sh` is this project's docs gate. It fails if an unstamped
  `{{`-style placeholder survived bootstrap, if a shared-layer file named in
  `VERSION` is missing, or if this manual references a repo path that does not
  exist.
- `.githooks/pre-push` runs that gate before every push. It is wired by
  `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`, which bootstrap already ran — no hook
  manager, no dependency.

Run the gate yourself at any time with `sh scripts/check.sh`.
